      "speaker_id": "narrator",
      "text": "Vishnu rose to meet Madhu and Kaitabha.\n\nNo army marched into the waters. No ranks gathered behind him. Vishnu met the two Asuras with his arms, and the combat closed around them.\n\nThe two Asuras turned from the lotus to face him."
    },
    {
      "badge_number": 2,
      "box": {
        "height": 0.11,
        "width": 0.84,
        "x": 0.08,
        "y": 0.54
      },
      "channel": "NARRATION",
      "font": {
        "minimum_size": 22,
        "size": 22
      },
      "lettering_id": "p13-narration-b",
      "padding": 12,
      "panel_id": "p13-panel-03",
      "placement_scope": "PAGE_BAND",
      "reading_order": 2,
      "source_script_hash": "d434e35c4bfe2edadab09a7b07c9a3e24a81ff2d838b9f0aeed99ce3d54be4f6",
      "speaker_id": "narrator",
      "text": "Brahma’s danger had not vanished; it had become a confrontation. Yoganidra had answered the invocation by withdrawing, appearing before Brahma, and opening the way for Vishnu to wake.\n\nNow the long struggle began."
    }
  ],
